From d065fd674eca239c6a62af8322bb394d3bc45a53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emergent E3 <e3@nivxray.local>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:15:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] N-3A: normalise BSON in the telemetry recent response

GET /api/telemetry/frontend/recent returned raw Mongo documents to the
response serializer, normalising only the top-level _id and recorded_at. A
single stored nested ObjectId, Decimal128 or non-UTF-8 Binary therefore
became an unauthenticated 500 (N-3).

_json_safe() coerces recursively with explicit, lossless rules: ObjectId to
hex, Decimal128/Decimal to an exact string (never float), bytes to base64
(never a UTF-8 guess), datetimes to ISO-8601, unanticipated BSON types to
str. JSON-native values, field names, key order, limit and ordering are
unchanged; nothing is dropped and no exception is suppressed.

Endpoint-scoped: no global encoder, no change to the other two N-3 routes,
no authentication or tenant change. The route remains unauthenticated (N-2).

(cherry picked from commit 38e294c614456406c0198163d896afb03f8575f9)
